<task id="094" project="ebilling-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>Submit Invoice from a source Document: all-or-nothing steps 1-6, file first (A), copy rule (B), 050a re-file retired</title>
    <phase>3 Procedures and files (WP3, EB-D-148) — wave W3-E</phase>
    <gate>blocked until 086, 090 and 098 are done</gate>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Changes the invoice write path and an authorized BFF route (tags bff-api, auth); secure-record isolation and an undo of committed rows; deps on 3 tasks.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>opus</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Auth and tenant-isolation code (copy rule, isolation re-run) plus all-or-nothing ordering with races between commit, re-run, flip and undo (model 9.1, reviews section 7).</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>P3-E</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>false</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>Edits InvoiceSubmissionService, InvoiceSubmissionPersister and InvoiceSubmissionAfterSteps, which 095 and 097 extend next; nothing else in P3-E touches them, but run it alone in the Submission folder.</parallel-reason>
    <deps>086, 090, 092, 098</deps>
    <tags>bff-api, api, auth, finance, write-path, secure-records, job</tags>
    <estimated-effort>3-4 days</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Turn 050a's existing-document submission into Submit Invoice (model section 9.1, EB-D-148): the source Document (an email attachment Document, or a confirmed document) never moves; its bytes are copied into the new invoice's Stored File (Invoice PDF, Firm-visible = No, source document and communication recorded) through steps 1-6 of 9.1, all or nothing. File an unfiled communication first (A). The copy rule (B) is served by 090's internal download route from the source ids this task writes. The 050a re-file (InvoiceDocumentRefile, owner change, share mirroring) is retired.</prompt>

  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Expert in the Dataverse write path (ADR-002), ExecuteTransaction with IfRowVersionMatches, secure-record isolation (uac-r2) and idempotent job steps. Follow ADRs strictly.</role>

  <goal>An internal caller submits a source Document as an invoice; the job stages a copy, commits invoice + lines + approval + Stored File (Not yet servable) in one transaction guarded on the source version, re-runs the isolation check before any after-step, and either flips the file to Servable and runs the after-steps, or undoes every row and the blob and leaves the submission Failed. No path moves or re-owns the source Document.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>The contract is projects/ebilling-r1/notes/procedure-and-file-model.md section 9.1 (all of it) with notes/procedure-model-reviews.md section 7; read both first. Code (verified 2026-10-21): SubmitExistingDocumentAsync (InvoiceSubmissionService.cs:305), DecideAsync (:724), dedupe id per notes/050a-confirm-redirect.md section 2; ResolveFilingAsync and ExistingDocumentIsolationCheck.CheckAsync (:99) with RecordThreadFiling.ParentsOf (Services/Dataverse/RecordThreadFiling.cs:59); BuildExistingDocumentGuard (InvoiceSubmissionPersister.cs:497-513); resume (:238-240 to ResumeAsync); the 050a re-file step (InvoiceSubmissionAfterSteps.cs:326-352); the verified-pointer byte read (InvoiceSubmissionProcessingJobHandler.cs:535-548); SecureChildShareSynchronizer.SecureRootsAboveAsync; RefileCommunicationAsync behind PATCH /api/communications/{id}/filing (Api/CommunicationEndpoints.cs:133). Deps: 090 file store (staging, row, If-Match flip, internal download route with the copy rule, orphan reconcile, detector); 086 secure child registration of invoice Stored Files; 098 the (a′) predicate reading the Submit Invoice source.</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="modify">Under src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Finance/Submission/: InvoiceSubmissionService.cs (step 1), InvoiceSubmissionContracts.cs (communication id), InvoiceSubmissionPersister.cs (step 4), InvoiceSubmissionAfterSteps.cs (steps 5-6 replace :326-352), AdminAttentionText.cs</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Jobs/Handlers/InvoiceSubmissionProcessingJobHandler.cs (steps 2-3)</file>
      <file role="new">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Finance/Submission/SubmitInvoiceIsolationRerun.cs (step 5 and the undo; name directional)</file>
      <file role="delete">Services/Finance/Submission/InvoiceDocumentRefile.cs and its registration in Infrastructure/DI/FinanceModule.cs</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/Finance/InvoiceSubmissionEndpoints.cs (route) and FinanceEndpoints.cs:41 (confirm delegates)</file>
      <file role="new">tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/Services/Finance/Submission/SubmitInvoiceIsolationRerunTests.cs; the existing Submission tests there are updated</file>
      <file role="modify">tests/integration/contract/Api/Finance/InvoiceSubmissionEndpointsContractTests.cs, FinanceEndpointsAuthorizationContractTests.cs</file>
    </relevant-files>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="model 9.1 step 1 (#2150, D-140)">Every request: the caller's own Read on the source document and its communication (gate variant, GetCallerRightsForRecordsAsync); Read and AppendTo on the core record. An unfiled communication is filed to the target core record first (A, the RefileCommunicationAsync core, with the caller's rights) and its thread resolved before the D-140 pre-check. 409 ebilling.submission.document_core_record_mismatch; 503 on a read fault; nothing but A is written before the submission row.</constraint>
    <constraint source="model 9.1 steps 2-6">Implement steps 2-6 exactly as model 9.1 words them. Points a literal reading must not miss: Stored File id = f(submission id, source versionnumber) with the persister's SHA-256 IdOf scheme, version and SHA recorded at staging; the step-3 flags (Restricted, internal-only, privacy) are never refusal grounds and never stored, and an unreadable one fails the submission; step 4's one transaction holds the Stored File row (Not yet servable, Firm-visible No, Invoice PDF, source ids) and the IfRowVersionMatches guard at the STAGED version, with re-stage-and-retry on a guard fault and blob deletion on a transaction fault; it never writes sprk_document.sprk_invoice, the document's owner or its shares; step 5 runs before totals, Signals, Decision Record, indexing and notification, and any fault in it is a failure; undo order is Stored File row and blob, approval, lines, invoice, then clear sprk_FirmInvoiceNumber, sprk_PONumber, sprk_FindingsJson and sprk_Invoice, keeping Failed, the admin note and the correlation; A's filing survives and the admin note says so; undo is complete or held; resume runs step 5 and the flip first and never flips twice.</constraint>
    <constraint source="model 9.1, 12 (050a row)">The 050a re-file is retired: InvoiceDocumentRefile, its after-step and its admin-attention "document NOT filed" wording are removed; the D-140 chain, the isolation check and the dedupe id are kept. The confirm route stays and calls the same operation.</constraint>
    <constraint source="model 9.1 Sources, 9.2 (owner K)">Isolated sources (internal-only, Restricted, Private thread) are allowed; the copy stays Firm-visible No and out of indexing, search and chat grounding.</constraint>
    <constraint source="model 5.3 (099)">The Submit Invoice route sits in the /api/finance group and inherits step 0 (flagged-external caller refused before any record read).</constraint>
    <constraint source="CLAUDE.md §10">BFF hygiene per .claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md: placement stated, publish-size delta against a fresh master build, no new package, no new HIGH CVE.</constraint>
    <constraint source="live data">No live Dataverse writes and no deploys.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <files>
      <file>projects/ebilling-r1/notes/procedure-and-file-model.md (sections 4.1, 4.3, 5.1, 9.1, 9.2)</file>
      <file>projects/ebilling-r1/notes/procedure-model-reviews.md (sections 7, 14)</file>
      <file>projects/ebilling-r1/notes/050a-confirm-redirect.md (sections 2-4: what is kept and what is retired)</file>
