      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-002-thin-plugins.md, ADR-004-job-contract.md, ADR-008-endpoint-filters.md, ADR-028-spaarke-auth-architecture.md</file>
      <file>.claude/patterns/api/endpoint-filters.md; .claude/patterns/testing/unit-test-structure.md</file>
      <file>docs/architecture/DATAVERSE-WRITE-PATH-ARCHITECTURE.md; docs/standards/TEST-ARCHITECTURE.md</file>
    </files>
    <patterns>
      <pattern name="Guard and resume to copy" location="src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Finance/Submission/">BuildExistingDocumentGuard (Persister :497-513) re-pointed at the staged version; ResumeAsync's Retry shape (AfterSteps :233-269) for step 5.</pattern>
    </patterns>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0">Declare FULL. Read 090's, 086's and 098's notes and code (file store API, flip, registration, the column (a′) reads as the source). Grep clients of /api/finance/invoice-review/confirm.</step>
    <step order="1">Step 1 and the route (name directional: POST /api/finance/invoice-submissions/from-document, keyed on communication and document); confirm calls the same operation.</step>
    <step order="2">Steps 2-3 in the job; step 4 in the persister.</step>
    <step order="3">Steps 5-6 replace the re-file step; delete InvoiceDocumentRefile, its registration and tests; AdminAttentionText for the new outcomes.</step>
    <step order="4">Tests per the acceptance criteria; the two seeding proofs; build; Finance and Submission unit tests; full ArchTests; publish-size delta.</step>
    <step order="5">Notes in projects/ebilling-r1/notes/094-submit-invoice.md: step order, each failure's outcome (table like 050a section 4), seeding proofs, §11 answers.</step>
    <step order="6">Update TASK-INDEX.md: this task's status cell to `✅ [done]` after the adversarial reviews and uac-r2's review.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If the Stored File row cannot join 049's ExecuteTransaction (for example 086's ForParents owner cannot be resolved before the transaction), STOP and report; do not commit the file row separately.</trigger>
    <trigger>If 090's flip cannot check blob existence and SHA inside the If-Match write, STOP and report to 090's owner rather than flipping without the check.</trigger>
    <trigger>If 092 has not landed and extraction still reads bytes from the source Document's SPE pointer, STOP and ask whether extraction reads the staged copy here or waits for 092.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <justification>
    <existing>InvoiceSubmissionService.SubmitExistingDocumentAsync (:305) and the confirm route (FinanceEndpoints.cs:41) submit an existing document; InvoiceDocumentRefile moves it under the invoice.</existing>
    <extension>Yes for the operation: the existing-document entry is extended, not duplicated. One new route, because the confirm route's filter needs Write on the document (a re-file) and its body has no communication; Submit Invoice needs Read on the document and its communication and the (communication, document) key (model 9.1). One new class for step 5 and the undo, because the after-steps have no undo of committed rows today.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>Without it the source Document is re-owned under the invoice (owner and share change), invoice bytes never reach the file store, and a source refiled or made Secure between check and commit leaves an invoice readable outside its isolation (reviews section 7 races a-e).</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <tools>
    <tool name="dotnet">build, test</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">InvoiceSubmissionService, InvoiceSubmissionContracts, InvoiceSubmissionProcessingJobHandler, InvoiceSubmissionPersister, InvoiceSubmissionAfterSteps, SubmitInvoiceIsolationRerun.cs, InvoiceSubmissionEndpoints, FinanceEndpoints (confirm); InvoiceDocumentRefile.cs deleted</output>
    <output type="test">SubmitInvoiceIsolationRerunTests.cs and the updated Submission unit and Finance contract tests</output>
    <output type="docs">projects/ebilling-r1/notes/094-submit-invoice.md</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Happy path: a submission from a source Document creates invoice, lines, approval and one Stored File (purpose Invoice PDF, Firm-visible No, source document, source communication, source version and SHA set) that ends Servable; the source Document's owner, shares, sprk_invoice link and bytes are unchanged (test).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Authorization, each before any submission write: caller without Read on the source document → refused; without Read on its communication → refused; without Read and AppendTo on the core record → 403; a flagged-external caller → refused by step 0 before any record read; unauthenticated → 401 (tests).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">A: an unfiled communication is filed to the target core record before the pre-check, with the caller's rights; a caller without Write on the communication gets the refile's refusal and no submission; after a later step-5 undo the filing remains and the admin note says so (tests).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Step 1 answers: document filed under another core record → 409 ebilling.submission.document_core_record_mismatch; a chain read fault → 503; nothing written (tests).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Step 4: a source write between staging and commit faults the guard; the job re-stages under the new version's id and commits once; a transaction failure deletes the staged blob (tests).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Step 5 fail: the source refiled to another core record between commit and re-run, or SecureRootsAboveAsync(source) differing from the Stored File's roots, or a fault in the re-run → Stored File row and blob, approval, lines and invoice deleted in that order; the four submission columns cleared; submission Failed with admin note and correlation; no Signal, Decision Record, indexing job or notification written (tests).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Undo held: a delete fault leaves the submission Failed and the Stored File Not yet servable; a later compensation run completes it (test).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Step 6: a resume after a commit whose step 5 never ran runs step 5 and the flip before any other after-step; a resume of an already-Servable file does not flip again (tests).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Copy rule end to end: after a successful submission, a caller who loses Read on the source document is refused the copy on 090's internal download route (test using 090's route).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Retired: InvoiceDocumentRefile and its after-step are gone; no code path writes sprk_document.sprk_invoice, reassigns the source's owner or mirrors its shares for a Submit Invoice (grep plus test).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Seeding proofs, recorded in notes: (1) make the step-5 re-run report Pass unconditionally → the refiled-source undo test fails; (2) skip the Stored File delete in the undo → the undo test fails; both restored.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">dotnet build exits 0; Finance and Submission unit tests and the full ArchTests pass (known pre-existing failures listed by name); publish-size delta recorded; no new HIGH CVE.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Cover the stated contract plus the edge cases named above. Anything beyond that needs a one-line justification in task notes.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>Reviews: adversarial-reviewer twice (auth, tenant isolation) and uac-r2 (model 14). Wave order puts 092 before 094 (W3-C); it is not a declared dep. Known limits carried from the model (owner-visible): a change after step 5 passes (O-32, uac-r2 K2), K3 soft delete 7 days, K4, K6; the D-139 rule that an ended submission blocks a re-submit of the same document is kept from 050a. The guard's live version-bump proof is still outstanding (model section 15, Engineering). OWNER 2026-10-21 (re-plan Q1): the email UI is task 118 (toolbar Submit Invoice replacing Link Invoice, flagged attachments via the profile's sprk_documenttype = Invoice, Email Review Invoice tab). This task is server-only; record the final route name, request (communication, invoice document, supporting documents) and error codes in its notes for 118. ontology-r1 088 gate 2026-10-22, F1 for this task: deleting a source document deletes its SPE file first (DocumentCheckoutService.DeleteCoreAsync), and the row delete then fails with a 500 because the Stored File's Restrict lookup refuses it. The 188d 409 pre-check counts only _sprk_parentdocument_value (also DataverseDocumentsEndpoints.cs:354). Model section 5.2 promises a 409 for Stored File references. Fix here: extend the pre-check on all three document delete routes to also count sprk_storedfile rows whose _sprk_sourcedocument_value equals the document, and return the same document_has_child_documents 409 before any file is deleted. Must-fire test per route: a document referenced by a Stored File returns 409 and its SPE file is untouched. Must-not-fire: an unreferenced document deletes as before. Also see 095 for the email source. 088 retype 2026-10-22: sprk_storedfile.sprk_sourceversion is String(20) and sprk_sizebytes is Integer (files over 2 GiB cannot be stored). The source document's row version is written in the ONE canonical string form owned by 090's constraint (invariant culture, no padding, no separators), the same string used for StoredFileIds.ForSourceVersion; this task's guard reads it in that form.</notes>

  <execution>
    <skill>.claude/skills/task-execute/SKILL.md</skill>
    <protocol>Load every file in knowledge/files before Step 1. Follow task-execute for rigor, checkpoints and quality gates.</protocol>
  </execution>
</task>
